From 0b8a462d3bd14371dc536ceb993d2cf3db29f07c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vita-build <vita@build>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:10:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vita: batching by index lists (no shader change), framebuffer
 binds only when they change, texture decoding by time

- vitaGL's compiler took no change to the draw vertex shader (t20, t21: even plain ifs), so t21's
  batch programs are gone. GlGpu::LayerBatch draws the classes from index lists (unsigned short,
  per window of up to 65532 vertices with the attributes starting at the window's first): the
  opaque faces' true depth, their colour, then semi-transparent, then subtractive, with the
  draw programs t17 had (u_dpass 0/1 as before).
- BindFb/SetViewport: glBindFramebuffer and glViewport only when the framebuffer or viewport
  changes (forgotten at each swap). Every draw used to bind its target again; if vitaGL starts a
  scene on each bind the whole target is loaded and stored per draw, which would grow with the
  resolution and the draw count (t21: GPU swap 40-80 ms at 960x544, CPU draw up to 180 us a GL
  draw). THPS_GL_FBCACHE=0: as before. [gl] counts framebuffer binds a frame.
- Texture cache: 8 decodes a frame, then more while the frame's decoding took under
  THPS_GL_DECODEMS (default 25 ms). A triangle without a slot takes the per-pixel lookup, which
  at 960x544 made loading screens and menus 300-500 ms frames.
---
 platform/pc/README.md           |   2 +
 platform/pc/include/pc/gl_gpu.h |  28 ++-
 platform/pc/src/pc_gpu_gl.cpp   | 339 ++++++++++++++++----------------
 3 files changed, 178 insertions(+), 191 deletions(-)

diff --git a/platform/pc/README.md b/platform/pc/README.md
index cf848c9..583410f 100644
--- a/platform/pc/README.md
+++ b/platform/pc/README.md
@@ -562,6 +562,8 @@ window, `THPS_FAST`, `THPS_DETERMINISTIC`) never wait for a display.
 | `THPS_R3D_BATCH=0` | OpenGL ES (Vita): a native 3D layer's faces drawn in the PS1's order, split where they overlap (before t20); default: each run of faces between 2D primitives in one depth pass and one colour pass for the opaque faces, then the semi-transparent ones in order |
 | `THPS_VITA_RES=WxH` | Vita: screens drawn at most 512x240, 720x408 or 960x544 (default), scaled up to the screen |
 | `THPS_VITA_FPS=30` | Vita: every other frame shown (the game still runs at 60) |
+| `THPS_GL_FBCACHE=0` | OpenGL: bind the target framebuffer and set the viewport at every draw again (before t22); default: only when they change |
+| `THPS_GL_DECODEMS=n` | OpenGL ES: texture cache pages decoded a frame: 8, then more while the frame's decoding took under n ms (default 25; before t22: 8 only) |
 | `THPS_R3DSTATS=1` | once a second: native 3D faces, culled faces, draws, and calls left to the retail code |
 | `THPS_R3D_VERIFY=1` | check the native renderer's float vertices and back-face tests against retail's integers |
 | `THPS_R3D_NEARDROP=1` | drop faces crossing the near plane that the PS1 dropped (default: OpenGL clips them) |
